{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And I know that the king of Egypt will not give you leave to go.</b> If I do not show him My strong hand — that is, as long as I do not make known to him My strong hand, he will not give you leave to go." "<b>Will not give.</b> לָא יִשְׁבֹּק — like ״עַל כֵּן לֹא נְתַתִּיךָ״ (Genesis 20), ״וְלֹא נְתָנוֹ אֱלֹהִים לְהָרַע עִמָּדִי״ (ibid. 31) — all of them are the language of giving. And R. Jacob b. R. Menachem says <b>and not by a strong hand</b> — and not because his hand is strong, ״כִּי מֵאָז אֶשְׁלַח אֶת יָדִי וְהִכֵּיתִי אֶת מִצְרַיִם וגוֹ׳״, and they translate it ״וְלָא מִן קֳדָם דְחֵילֵהּ תַּקִּיף״. From the name of Rabbi Yaakov bar Rabbi Menachem it was told to me."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {1 "The abbreviation וְיֵ״מְ is resolved as וְיֵשׁ מְפָרְשִׁים ('and some explain'); the following words are attributed to Rabbi Yaakov bar Rabbi Menachem by name."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:28.203788602Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}